# ICMP Discovery

## ICMP Echo

ICMP Echo Requests are the packets commonly used by `ping`. A responding host sends an Echo Reply, but firewalls may block these requests.

```bash
sudo nmap -PE -sn 10.200.6.0/24
```

## ICMP Timestamp

Nmap can send ICMP Timestamp Requests and look for Timestamp Replies:

```bash
sudo nmap -PP -sn TARGETS
```

## ICMP Address Mask

Nmap can send ICMP Address Mask Requests:

```bash
sudo nmap -PM -sn TARGETS
```

These less commonly supported ICMP request types may be filtered or ignored by modern systems. Lack of a reply does not prove the host is down.

