# Masscan

Masscan is a high-speed port scanner that can scan large ranges quickly. It is more aggressive in its packet rate than many default Nmap scans, so use it carefully and only within authorized scope.

```bash
masscan 10.200.6.0/24 -p443
masscan 10.200.6.0/24 -p80,443
masscan 10.200.6.0/24 -p22-25
```

The `-p` option accepts a port, comma-separated list, or range. These examples scan for specified ports; they are not a replacement for every type of Nmap host-discovery scan.

